                <pb facs="0360" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg354"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Guzman to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Cablegram.—Translation.—Handed to Mr. Gresham by
                        Mr. Guzman November 24.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-11-23"><hi rendition="#italic">November 23,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>British Minister Gosling has telegraphed to Limon orders for an English
                    man-of-war to go to Bluefields. Bequest American Government to send also a
                    cruiser to that port. Very urgent.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Baca.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
